WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.542
<v Examiner>Exam case 3.

2
00:00:02.542 --> 00:00:03.202
<v Examiner>Asthma.

3
00:00:03.652 --> 00:00:06.020
<v Examiner>Ane has had severe asthma since they were young.

4
00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:09.129
<v Examiner>During a particularly bad attack, Ane has difficulty breathing,

5
00:00:09.129 --> 00:00:10.658
<v Examiner>particularly on the out-breath.

6
00:00:10.658 --> 00:00:15.050
<v Examiner>Ane's asthma is often triggered by small particles of pollen that make their way into the

7
00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:18.257
<v Examiner>lungs, despite the protective features designed to keep them out.

8
00:00:18.257 --> 00:00:20.625
<v Examiner>Ane makes sure to have their Salbutamol inhaler,

9
00:00:20.625 --> 00:00:22.895
<v Examiner>which helps relieve the symptoms of an attack.

10
00:00:23.345 --> 00:00:27.862
Case 3 is the biggest case in the exam, so it's split over three tracks.

11
00:00:27.862 --> 00:00:29.745
This one is the attack itself.

12
00:00:30.195 --> 00:00:30.716
<v Examiner>One mark.

13
00:00:30.716 --> 00:00:33.672
<v Examiner>What term is used to describe difficulty breathing?

14
00:00:34.122 --> 00:00:34.757
Dyspnoea.

15
00:00:34.757 --> 00:00:37.650
Dys means bad, and pnoea means breathing.

16
00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:40.684
Compare eupnoea, which is normal breathing.

17
00:00:40.684 --> 00:00:41.883
Tachypnoea, fast.

18
00:00:41.883 --> 00:00:43.294
Apnoea, none at all.

19
00:00:43.294 --> 00:00:49.503
And hyperventilation, breathing hard and fast, which changes the blood's carbon dioxide.

20
00:00:49.953 --> 00:00:50.616
<v Examiner>Three marks.

21
00:00:50.616 --> 00:00:53.985
<v Examiner>What is happening in Ane's lungs to make breathing difficult?

22
00:00:54.435 --> 00:00:56.023
Three things, a mark each.

23
00:00:56.023 --> 00:00:57.977
The hook: squeeze, swell, slime.

24
00:00:58.427 --> 00:01:02.931
Bronchoconstriction: the smooth muscle around the airway has contracted,

25
00:01:02.931 --> 00:01:04.746
so the airway is constricted.

26
00:01:04.746 --> 00:01:08.500
Inflammation: the wall of the airway is thick with swelling.

27
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.379
And increased mucus secretion, which leaves less room for air.

28
00:01:13.829 --> 00:01:14.459
<v Examiner>Two marks.

29
00:01:14.459 --> 00:01:18.053
<v Examiner>How are Ane's ventilation and airway resistance affected?

30
00:01:18.503 --> 00:01:21.575
Airway resistance is high, so it's harder to breathe.

31
00:01:21.575 --> 00:01:26.211
It takes a greater pressure difference to move the air, and that's the dyspnoea.

32
00:01:26.211 --> 00:01:30.906
And the accessory respiratory muscles are recruited: extra muscles for breathing.

33
00:01:30.906 --> 00:01:34.268
Her phrase for it is an increase in the work of breathing.

34
00:01:34.718 --> 00:01:35.256
<v Examiner>One mark.

35
00:01:35.256 --> 00:01:38.899
<v Examiner>How does an inhaler help when Ane is having an asthma attack?

36
00:01:39.349 --> 00:01:43.245
A reliever inhaler, like Salbutamol, is a bronchodilator.

37
00:01:43.245 --> 00:01:48.781
It forces the smooth muscle of the airways to relax, which lets the airway widen,

38
00:01:48.781 --> 00:01:52.198
and that relieves the symptoms so Ane can breathe.

39
00:01:52.198 --> 00:01:57.803
Don't mix it up with a preventer, which is a corticosteroid: an anti-inflammatory.

40
00:01:59.253 --> 00:02:02.859
Her formative test asks the same things as drop-downs.

41
00:02:02.859 --> 00:02:04.929
Difficulty breathing: dyspnoea.

42
00:02:04.929 --> 00:02:10.339
The bronchi and bronchioles become obstructed by swelling and mucus accumulation.

43
00:02:10.339 --> 00:02:13.077
And the inhaler makes the airways dilate.

44
00:02:13.527 --> 00:02:14.167
<v Examiner>Once more.

45
00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:14.999
<v Examiner>Ane's attack.

46
00:02:17.449 --> 00:02:21.206
Difficulty breathing is dyspnoea: dys, bad, pnoea, breathing.

47
00:02:21.206 --> 00:02:26.750
Three things narrow Ane's airways: bronchoconstriction, with the smooth muscle contracted;

48
00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:29.953
inflammation, a swollen airway wall; and more mucus.

49
00:02:29.953 --> 00:02:34.204
Airway resistance is high, so it needs a greater pressure difference,

50
00:02:34.204 --> 00:02:38.146
and the accessory muscles are recruited: more work of breathing.

51
00:02:38.146 --> 00:02:40.179
The reliever is a bronchodilator:

52
00:02:40.179 --> 00:02:43.690
it relaxes the airway smooth muscle so the airway widens.

53
00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:47.017
A preventer is a corticosteroid, an anti-inflammatory.
